# Memory System

**GOAL**: Use basic-memory and cursor-history tools directly for simple, effective knowledge management without custom wrappers.

## Memory System Setup

**Create this folder structure in every project:**

```
memories/
├── knowledge/         # Facts, learnings, documentation
├── plans/             # Goals, roadmaps, strategies
├── decisions/         # ADRs (Architectural Decision Records)
├── tasks/             # Task management, todos
├── conversations/     # AI conversation exports (from chi)
├── notes/             # Daily notes, observations
└── lessons-learned/   # What worked, what didn't, retrospectives
```

## Direct Tool Usage

**Use these tools directly - no custom commands needed:**

### Basic-Memory (bm) Commands

```bash
# Create notes
bm --project "project-name" tool write-note --title "Title" --folder "knowledge" --content "Content"

# Search memories
bm --project "project-name" tool search-notes "query"

# Read specific note
bm --project "project-name" tool read-note "note-title"

# List all notes
bm --project "project-name" tool list-notes

# Set up new project
bm project add "project-name" "~/path/to/project/memories"
```

### Cursor-History (chi) Commands

```bash
# Interactive conversation selection
chi --select

# Export latest conversation
chi

# Export for specific workspace
chi --workspace "project-name"

# Browse all conversations
chi --browse
```

## Content Routing

**Route content to appropriate folders:**

| Content Type                | Destination                 | Example                      |
| --------------------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| **Facts & Learnings**       | `memories/knowledge/`       | "React hooks best practices" |
| **Plans & Strategies**      | `memories/plans/`           | "Q1 2024 roadmap"            |
| **Architectural Decisions** | `memories/decisions/`       | "ADR-001: Database choice"   |
| **Task Management**         | `memories/tasks/`           | "Implement user auth"        |
| **AI Conversations**        | `memories/conversations/`   | "Design discussion with AI"  |
| **Daily Notes**             | `memories/notes/`           | "2024-01-15 progress"        |
| **Lessons Learned**         | `memories/lessons-learned/` | "What worked in sprint 1"    |

## File Standards

**Every markdown file MUST include YAML frontmatter:**

```yaml
---
title: "File Title"
description: "Brief description of content"
created: "2024-01-15"
tags: ["tag1", "tag2"]
status: "active" # or "completed", "archived"
---
```

## Daily Workflow

**Simple daily process:**

1. **Start**: Check `memories/plans/` for current priorities
2. **Work**: Use `bm` to save learnings as you work
3. **Export**: Use `chi` to save important conversations
4. **Review**: Use `bm` to search and find relevant information

## MCP Integration

**In Cursor, use basic-memory MCP tools directly:**

- `mcp_basic-memory_write_note` - Create new notes
- `mcp_basic-memory_search_notes` - Search existing notes
- `mcp_basic-memory_read_note` - Read specific notes
- `mcp_basic-memory_list_notes` - List all notes

**REMEMBER**: Use the tools directly as designed. No custom wrappers needed. Keep it simple and leverage the power of basic-memory and cursor-history.
